Spec: Layer Panel

Purpose:
  Allow users to manage multiple laser layers — create, rename, reorder,
  toggle visibility, and assign shapes to layers.

Owns:
  ./LayersPanel.tsx
  ./LayersPanel.test.tsx

Can modify:
  ../../store/slices/shapes.ts
  ../../types/layer.ts

Must:
  Display all layers in a scrollable list.
  Show layer color swatch, name, and visibility toggle.
  Active layer is visually highlighted.
  Clicking a layer makes it the active layer (new shapes go here).
  Double-click layer name to rename inline.
  Drag-and-drop reorders layers.
  Eye icon toggles layer visibility (hidden layers don't render).
  Add Layer button creates a new layer with unique name and color.
  Delete layer moves its shapes to the default layer (cannot delete last layer).
  Shapes inherit the active layer's color when created.

Must not:
  Allow deleting the last remaining layer.
  Allow two layers with the same ID.
  Modify shape geometry when changing layer assignment.
  Import laser power/speed settings (out of scope).

Depends on:
  @useStore (layers, activeLayerId, setLayers, setActiveLayerId)
  @LaserLayer type
  @CanvasRenderer (respects layer visibility)

Scenario: create a new layer
  Given 1 default layer exists
  When the user clicks "Add Layer"
  Then a second layer appears in the list
  And it becomes the active layer
  And new shapes are assigned to this layer

Scenario: hide a layer
  Given Layer 2 has 3 shapes visible on canvas
  When the user clicks the visibility toggle on Layer 2
  Then those 3 shapes disappear from the canvas
  And they are preserved in the store (not deleted)

Scenario: delete layer redistributes shapes
  Given Layer 2 has 2 shapes and Layer 1 is the default
  When the user deletes Layer 2
  Then the 2 shapes move to Layer 1
  And Layer 2 is removed from the list

Tasks:
  [ ] Create LayersPanel React component.
  [ ] Implement layer list with color swatch and name.
  [ ] Add active layer highlighting and click-to-activate.
  [ ] Add inline rename on double-click.
  [ ] Add visibility toggle (eye icon).
  [ ] Add "Add Layer" button with unique color generation.
  [ ] Add "Delete Layer" with shape redistribution.
  [ ] Update CanvasRenderer to skip hidden layers.
  [ ] Update shape creation to use activeLayerId.
  [ ] Add drag-and-drop reordering.
  [ ] Add unit tests for layer CRUD operations.
  [ ] Integrate into RightSidebar as a tab.

Done when:
  Users can create, rename, reorder, hide, and delete layers.
  Shapes render only when their layer is visible.
  Layer state persists in .laser project files.
  Cannot delete the last layer.
